    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/VascularMalformationsAndFistulas> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Acquired degenerative dilation or expansion (ectasia) of normal BLOOD VESSELS, often associated with aging. They are isolated, tortuous, thin-walled vessels and sources of bleeding. They occur most often in mucosal capillaries of the GASTROINTESTINAL TRACT leading to GASTROINTESTINAL HEMORRHAGE and ANEMIA." ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D016888> ;
