    <https://universalevidence.com/ontology/bearer> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/subjects/Population> .

<https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/BartterSyndrome>
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-06-12"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D001477> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://universalevidence.com/ontology/State> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/InbornErrorsOfMetabolism> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A group of disorders caused by defective salt reabsorption in the ascending LOOP OF HENLE. It is characterized by severe salt-wasting, HYPOKALEMIA; HYPERCALCIURIA; metabolic ALKALOSIS, and hyper-reninemic HYPERALDOSTERONISM without HYPERTENSION. There are several subtypes including ones due to mutations in the renal specific SODIUM-POTASSIUM-CHLORIDE SYMPORTERS." ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D001477> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Bartter syndrome" ;
    <https://universalevidence.com/ontology/bearer> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/subjects/Population> .

