<https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/ImmuneComplexDiseases>
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-06-16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007105> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://universalevidence.com/ontology/State> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/AllergicAndHypersensitivityDisorders> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Group of diseases mediated by the deposition of large soluble complexes of antigen and antibody with resultant damage to tissue. Besides SERUM SICKNESS and the ARTHUS REACTION, evidence supports a pathogenic role for immune complexes in many other IMMUNE SYSTEM DISEASES including GLOMERULONEPHRITIS, systemic lupus erythematosus (LUPUS ERYTHEMATOSUS, SYSTEMIC) and POLYARTERITIS NODOSA." ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007105> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Immune complex diseases" ;
    <https://universalevidence.com/ontology/bearer> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/subjects/Population> .

<https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/ImmuneReconstitutionInflammatorySyndrome>
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-06-17"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D054019> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://universalevidence.com/ontology/State> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/ImmuneSystemDiseases> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D018746> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Exuberant inflammatory response towards a previously acquired or undiagnosed opportunistic infection. It is frequently seen in AIDS patients following antiretroviral treatment." ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D054019> ;
