<https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/KlinefelterSyndrome>
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-06-16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007713> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://universalevidence.com/ontology/State> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/Hypogonadism> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A form of male HYPOGONADISM, characterized by the presence of an extra X CHROMOSOME, small TESTES, seminiferous tubule dysgenesis, elevated levels of GONADOTROPINS, low serum TESTOSTERONE, underdeveloped secondary sex characteristics, and male infertility (INFERTILITY, MALE). Patients tend to have long legs and a slim, tall stature. GYNECOMASTIA is present in many of the patients. The classic form has the karyotype 47,XXY. Several karyotype variants include 48,XXYY; 48,XXXY; 49,XXXXY, and mosaic patterns ( 46,XY/47,XXY; 47,XXY/48,XXXY, etc.)." ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007713> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Klinefelter syndrome" ;
    <https://universalevidence.com/ontology/bearer> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/subjects/Population> .

