    skos:definition "The composition, diversity, abundance, and structure of microbial communities associated with a host or a defined biological site, regardless of anatomical location." ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D064307> ;
    skos:inScheme state: ;
    skos:prefLabel "Microbiome composition" ;
    skos:scopeNote "Site-neutral umbrella for host-associated microbiomes, including oral, respiratory, vaginal, blood, skin, and multi-site communities. Use gastrointestinal microbiome status for gut, intestinal, fecal, or stool communities; use dysbiosis when a pathological imbalance is asserted; use bacterial load for a quantity or concentration without community composition." ;
    ue:bearer <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/subjects/Population> .

