<https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/Mycetoma>
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-06-16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D008271> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://universalevidence.com/ontology/State> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/Dermatomycoses> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A chronic progressive subcutaneous infection caused by species of fungi (eumycetoma), or actinomycetes (actinomycetoma). It is characterized by tumefaction, abscesses, and tumor-like granules representing microcolonies of pathogens, such as MADURELLA fungi and bacteria ACTINOMYCETES, with different grain colors." ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D008271> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Mycetoma" ;
    <https://universalevidence.com/ontology/bearer> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/subjects/Population> .

