    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Dilation of pupils to greater than 6 mm combined with failure of the pupils to constrict when stimulated with light. This condition may occur due to injury of the pupillary fibers in the oculomotor nerve, in acute angle-closure glaucoma, and in ADIE SYNDROME." ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D015878> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/> ;
