    skos:prefLabel "Trust in government" ;
    skos:scopeNote "Use for public confidence in government as a whole or in national, regional, or local government. Use InstitutionalTrust when the object is multiple or unspecified public institutions, and use the target-specific trust concept when the object is a central bank, police, science, or another separately modeled institution." ;
    ue:bearer <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/subjects/Population> .

state:TrustinScience a skos:Concept,
        ue:State ;
    dcterms:created "2026-06-18"^^xsd:date ;
    skos:altLabel "Confidence in science",
        "Scientific trust" ;
    skos:broader state:InstitutionalTrust ;
    skos:definition "The degree of confidence in the reliability, competence, and integrity of the scientific enterprise, including its knowledge claims and methods, scientists, and research institutions." ;
    skos:inScheme state: ;
    skos:prefLabel "Trust in science" ;
    skos:scopeNote "Use for trust judgments about science as a knowledge-producing enterprise, scientists generally, or scientific and research organizations. Use ScienceLiteracy for understanding science, ScientificEvidenceUse for the credibility or use of particular evidence, and broader attitude concepts for interest, enthusiasm, stereotypes, or career preferences without a trust judgment; use target-specific concepts such as VaccineTrust or AIAcceptance when the object is a vaccine or artificial-intelligence system rather than science generally." ;
    ue:bearer <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/subjects/Population> .

state:TrustintheCentralBank a skos:Concept,
        ue:State ;
    dcterms:created "2026-06-18"^^xsd:date ;
    skos:altLabel "Central bank trust",
        "Confidence in the central bank" ;
    skos:broader state:InstitutionalTrust ;
    skos:definition "The degree of public confidence in the central bank's competence, integrity, and ability to maintain monetary and financial stability." ;
    skos:inScheme state: ;
    skos:prefLabel "Trust in the central bank" ;
    skos:scopeNote "Use for public confidence in a central bank as an institution, including confidence in its competence, integrity, or ability to maintain monetary and financial stability. Do not use for central-bank independence alone, forecast accuracy or reliance alone, inflation expectations or their anchoring, or central-bank communication interventions." ;
    ue:bearer <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/subjects/Population> .

state:TrustinthePolice a skos:Concept,
        ue:State ;
    dcterms:created "2026-06-18"^^xsd:date ;
    skos:altLabel "Police trust" ;
    skos:broader state:InstitutionalTrust ;
    skos:definition "The degree of public confidence that police act competently, fairly, lawfully, and in the public interest." ;
    skos:inScheme state: ;
    skos:prefLabel "Trust in the police" ;
    skos:related state:PoliceLegitimacy ;
    skos:scopeNote "Use for confidence in police competence, fairness, integrity, reliability, or public-interest conduct. Do not use for acceptance of police authority as rightful or an obligation to obey it (PoliceLegitimacy), or for broader composites of cooperation, satisfaction, conflict, conduct, and interaction quality (PolicePopulationRelations)." ;
    ue:bearer <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/subjects/Population> .

state:Trustworthiness a skos:Concept,
        ue:State ;
    dcterms:created "2026-06-18"^^xsd:date ;
    skos:altLabel "perceived trustworthiness" ;
    skos:broader state:SocialAndStrategicDecisionBehavior ;
    skos:definition "The actual or perceived reliability of a person, group, organization, or counterparty, including keeping commitments, reciprocating entrusted resources, and maintaining a reputation for dependable conduct." ;
    skos:inScheme state: ;
    skos:prefLabel "Trustworthiness" ;
    skos:scopeNote "Use for the trustee or counterparty quality, conduct, returned resources, or reputation, and for perceptions of that quality. Do not use for a trustor’s willingness to rely on someone, an amount sent by the trustor in a trust game, or generic confidence in a government, institution, technology, science, police, central bank, vaccine, or other named object when a target-specific trust concept exists." ;
    ue:bearer <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/subjects/Population> .

