<https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/GlobalDiseaseburden>
    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://universalevidence.com/ontology/Indicator> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "DALYs" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "GBD" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "disease burden" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D000087509> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Aggregate population-level measures of the total impact of diseases, injuries, and risk factors on health, typically expressed as disability-adjusted life years (DALYs) lost across populations and geographies." ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D000071219> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "IHME GBD estimates of DALYs attributable to ischemic heart disease by country and year." ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hiddenLabel> "burden of disease" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hiddenLabel> "global disease burden" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Global burden of disease" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/DiseasePrevalence> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/MaternalMortality> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/NeonatalMortality> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/states/UnderFiveMortality> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Refers to composite summary measures (e.g., DALYs, YLDs, YLLs) used to compare and track health loss across conditions and regions; distinct from condition-specific prevalence or mortality." ;
    <https://universalevidence.com/ontology/bearer> <https://universalevidence.com/vocab/subjects/Population> .

